 ## Background
-The triangular prism SDF is a standard primitive in the family of Signed Distance Functions for ray marching. It was popularized by Inigo Quilez in his online articles and code repositories on SDF primitives [S2, unofficial]. The specific implementation using absolute values and the constant $0.866025$ is a common optimization found in GLSL-based SDF libraries [S1, S2, unofficial].
+The formula is derived from the analytical solution for the distance to an equilateral triangle, extended to a prism by taking the maximum with the height constraint. It is commonly used in ray marching for procedural geometry.
 
